{"id":"34.3","doc":"T","title":"SD/MMC External Interface Signals","words":147,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The primary external interface signals, which enable the "},{"t":"block","v":"SD/MMC","id":"sdmmc"},{"t":"text","v":" controller to communicate with an external device, are clock (sdhost_cclk_out_1.eg:card1), command (sdhost_ccmd_out_1) and data signals (sdhost_cdata_in_1[7:0]/sdhost_cdata_out_1[7:0])."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Additional signals include the card interrupt, card detect, and write-protect signals."}]},{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The direction of each signal is shown in Figure 34.3-1."}]},{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The direction and description of each pin are listed in Table 34.3-1."}]}]},{"t":"fig","src":"images/trm-fig-34_3-1.png","alt":"Figure 34.3-1. SD/MMC Controller External Interface Signals","caption":"Figure 34.3-1. SD/MMC Controller External Interface Signals"},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 34.3-1. SD/MMC Signal Description","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Pin"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Direction"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Description"}]],"rows":[{"n":5,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_cclk_out"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Output"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Clock signals for slave device"}]]},{"n":6,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_ccmd"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Duplex"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Duplex command/response lines"}]]},{"n":7,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_cdata"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Duplex"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Duplex data read/write lines"}]]},{"n":8,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_card_detect_n"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Input"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Card detection input line"}]]},{"n":9,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_card_write_prt"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Input"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Card write protection status input"}]]},{"n":10,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_rst_n"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Output"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Hardware reset for MMC4.4 cards"}]]},{"n":11,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"sdhost_ccmd_od_pullup_en_n"}],[{"t":"text","v":"output"}],[{"t":"text","v":